      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There are pharmacological evidences that A(2B) receptors are involved in inflammatory processes, such as asthma. For this reason, many efforts has been made for identifying selective A(2B) antagonists as anti-asthmatic agents. The updated material related to this field has been rationalised and arranged in order to offer an overview of the topic."},
